            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already know పుస్తకం, a book, and you have held a short passage without translating every word. This lesson names the larger body that books and spoken works belong to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: వాఙ్మయం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వాఙ్మయం — vāṅmayaṁ — \"literature\", or more broadly, expression made of words."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it in three gentle pieces: vāṅ, ma, yaṁ. The first piece ends with the velar nasal heard in English sing. The spelling keeps that sound as ఙ్ before మ: వా-ఙ్-మ-యం."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word came through Sanskrit: vāc is speech, and maya means made of or filled with. A single పుస్తకం is one book; వాఙ్మయం (vāṅmayaṁ) is the world of words that books, speeches, and other verbal works make together."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One book, then the wider field it can belong to. The unusual spelling has had a meaning before it becomes a handwriting exercise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
