            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say వాఙ్మయం (vāṅmayaṁ) once. What does it mean? (\"Literature; the wider body of expression in words.\")"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now slow the first two pieces: vāṅ, ma. The letter between them is today's whole task."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ఙ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఙ — ṅa."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the velar nasal: the sound at the end of English sing. In వాఙ్మయం (vāṅmayaṁ), the vowel is suppressed, so ఙ్ leans into the following మ. The base letter you will write is ఙ (ṅa)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is an uncommon letter in modern Telugu words. That is why the book waited until it had given you a real word that needs it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ఙ — five small movements",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Follow the filmstrip slowly. Movements 1–3 stay joined: turn around the compact upper-left lobe, continue around the broad lower bowl, then curl up through the right lobe. Lift for the inner horizontal bar. Lift once more for the short downward headstroke."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The numbered route is one attested school-style order; Telugu handwriting can vary. Keep the three pen-down runs clear rather than racing the shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
